 "notes": "Each of the 8 EVENT830 series is listed in 5 ranges that skip the +-5 minute window around its 13:30Z close on the four calendar dates inside the window; the 4 others are one range. The candle job (period 1, one request per close, the 12 series' tickers batched, end_ts = close - 120 s, open_interest kept, weekdays only) is built by workers/oicand/oi_candles_job.py from the answers. The pacing and stop rules are as in SPXOI1_LISTS. Registration text: Desk A commit 29dd035e on claude/idea-desk-a, DESK_A_OICORE_PLACES_NOV13.md sha256 2d6301c6dfd25972f58293d6023c5ec1d2262791a46fe0d5f2899f68108d14d3 (twelve places, with the Head's 21:06Z dated line); the earlier nine place version is commit 560b645c, sha256 bce3242c1396454bc5237427dd9970b4a11bc007b9be51415b88bc52d626ec44. Pacing 5.0 seconds (12 requests a minute) on the Head's order of Nov 14, 2026; page budget 132 (44 requests, at most 3 pages each), about 11 minutes. Held-out guard copy HELDOUT_PULL_RUNS.md sha256 974f2713.",
 "status": "active",
 "host": "api.elections.kalshi.com",
 "base_path": "/trade-api/v2",
 "pacing_seconds": 5.0,
 "stop_rules": {
  "pause_seconds_on_429": "5, doubling to 60",
  "stop_after_consecutive_429": 3,
  "note": "a 429 is waited out with a doubling pause and the same request is asked again; three in a row end the run; no other address, no proxy, no retry around a refusal"
 }
